### Test requests for the backend.
### VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request" above each block.
### Rider / Visual Studio support .http files natively.
### Port 5080 = `dotnet run` locally AND the Docker Compose mapping, so these work for both.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@token = dummy-token

### Health (works today)
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "jordan", "password": "secret123" }

### Login — copy the "token" from the response into @token above once auth is real
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "jordan", "password": "secret123" }

### Me
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Active todos
GET {{host}}/api/todos?completed=false
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Completed todos
GET {{host}}/api/todos?completed=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create todo
POST {{host}}/api/todos
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Write the real TodosController", "categoryId": null }

### Complete a todo
PATCH {{host}}/api/todos/33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "isCompleted": true }

### Delete a todo
DELETE {{host}}/api/todos/33333333-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Categories
GET {{host}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create category
POST {{host}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Gym" }

### Validation error example (expect 400 ProblemDetails)
POST {{host}}/api/categories
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "" }
